<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Pasha Baban</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim Pasha Baban was a ruler of the Baban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>, a Kurdish principality in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrizor">Shahrizor</a>. In 1784 he founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulaymaniyah">Sulaymaniyah</a> as his new capital, naming it after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyuk-suleyman-pasha">Büyük Süleyman Pasha</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. Sulaymaniyah grew into a leading centre of Kurdish culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-pasha-baban.jpg" alt="Ibrahim Pasha Baban" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zamand Karim · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ibrahim_Pasha_Baban_Statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
